---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
---
<InfoPageLayout
  eyebrow="Commercial transparency"
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How HydroRigor separates compensated links, editorial links, and product-acquisition disclosures."
  pathname="/affiliate-disclosure/"
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' },
    { label: 'Testing Methodology', href: '/testing-methodology/' },
    { label: 'Buyer Guides', href: '/best/' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Current status</h2>
  <p>HydroRigor does not currently publish affiliate links or claim active affiliate relationships. M05 adds typed validation and rendering infrastructure, while the production merchant and commercial-destination registries remain empty. There are no paid links, tracking IDs, live prices, availability feeds, or affiliate accounts configured by this milestone.</p>

  <h2>Compensated-link standard</h2>
  <p>If a compensated relationship is separately approved and actually configured later, a clear disclosure must appear before or near its commercial links. Program-specific compensation language may be used only when it accurately reflects documented terms.</p>

  <h2>Link qualification</h2>
  <p>Compensated links must resolve through a typed merchant destination and include <code>sponsored</code> and <code>nofollow</code> relationship attributes. Ordinary source citations and editorial links are not labeled as compensated. HydroRigor does not cloak or shorten commercial destinations.</p>

  <h2>Separate acquisition disclosure</h2>
  <p>A supplied, loaned, or discounted product is a different material relationship from an affiliate link and requires its own disclosure. Neither relationship may determine which product is selected, how evidence is described, or what conclusion is reached.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
